2026-07-20T05:48:06.6810545Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6810776Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6811157Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6811469Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6811644Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6811855Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6812031Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6812237Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6812415Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6812639Z         def inc(x):
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6812829Z             return x + 1
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6813028Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6813184Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6813352Z         def test_answer():
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6813640Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6813854Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6814014Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6814177Z     To execute it::
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6814362Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6814520Z         $ pytest
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6814762Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6815050Z         collected 1 items
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6815256Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6815489Z         test_sample.py F
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6815685Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6815900Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6816233Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6816516Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6816690Z             def test_answer():
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6816918Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6817144Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6817359Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6817693Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6817877Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6818171Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6818456Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6818627Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6819294Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6820014Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6820174Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6820332Z     Features
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6820507Z     --------
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6820675Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6821114Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6821593Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6821765Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6822110Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6822522Z       of test modules and functions
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6822738Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6823026Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6823424Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6823769Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6824055Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6824412Z       test suites out of the box
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6824617Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6824786Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6824988Z     
2026-07-20T05:48:06.6825415Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
